Let's cross here.

247
00:08:59,864 --> 00:09:01,324
Oh, my. This place is...

248
00:09:01,824 --> 00:09:04,464
I've never been to this neighborhood.

249
00:09:04,534 --> 00:09:05,863
(It's also new to the Daughter of Nonhyeon.)

250
00:09:05,864 --> 00:09:06,903
Right.

251
00:09:06,904 --> 00:09:09,433
There's a mountain back there.

252
00:09:09,434 --> 00:09:10,533
- Over there?
- Over there.

253
00:09:10,534 --> 00:09:13,873
The mountain is in the back of my apartment complex.

254
00:09:13,874 --> 00:09:17,044
And there's an elementary school. So I attended that school.

255
00:09:17,374 --> 00:09:20,944
I attended that school until third grade.

256
00:09:21,244 --> 00:09:23,284
- Until third grade?
- Yes. Third grade.

257
00:09:23,914 --> 00:09:25,983
How old were you when you became a trainee?

258
00:09:25,984 --> 00:09:28,223
I was in 11th grade when I started.

259
00:09:28,224 --> 00:09:30,694
- You started late.
- Yes. I started quite late.

260
00:09:31,294 --> 00:09:33,063
Nayeon, you started when you were little.

261
00:09:33,064 --> 00:09:34,663
- I was in ninth grade.
- What?

262
00:09:34,664 --> 00:09:35,763
- You didn't start that early.
- Right.

263
00:09:35,764 --> 00:09:37,394
I didn't start that early.

264
00:09:37,864 --> 00:09:40,964
I became a trainee in ninth grade and trained for six years.

265
00:09:41,464 --> 00:09:42,733
- Six years?
- Yes.

266
00:09:42,734 --> 00:09:45,134
Right. You trained for a long time.

267
00:09:45,234 --> 00:09:47,803
- Six years.
- You know, training to become...

268
00:09:47,804 --> 00:09:50,074
- idol stars isn't an easy thing.
- It's not.

269
00:09:50,314 --> 00:09:52,243
You guys had monthly evaluations.

270
00:09:52,244 --> 00:09:54,013
- Right. You know it so well.
- If you don't do well...

271
00:09:54,014 --> 00:09:55,420
- Monthly evaluations...
- If you don't do well,

272
00:09:55,444 --> 00:09:57,113
- the supervisors would say...
- Monthly evaluations.

273
00:09:57,114 --> 00:09:58,553
"Today was your last day."

274
00:09:58,554 --> 00:10:00,953
- That's so true.
- They say that. They'd come in,

275
00:10:00,954 --> 00:10:03,354
- But everyone works so hard.
- put up a table, and leave.

276
00:10:03,524 --> 00:10:04,653
- On the bottom of the page, - Really?

277
00:10:04,654 --> 00:10:06,693
- 2 or 3 names would be there.
- Just like that?

278
00:10:06,694 --> 00:10:07,923
- Then you could get kicked out?
- Really?

279
00:10:07,924 --> 00:10:10,134
- We'd gather around and cry.
- You'd get kicked out.

280
00:10:10,434 --> 00:10:12,633
- Really?
- We waited while they evaluated us.

281
00:10:12,634 --> 00:10:13,663
Then they gave us the evaluation paper.

282
00:10:13,664 --> 00:10:15,003
Someone came in...

283
00:10:15,004 --> 00:10:16,503
- and put it up on the wall.
- No way.

284
00:10:16,504 --> 00:10:18,773
They ranked us from 1st to 10th place.

285
00:10:18,774 --> 00:10:21,003
The names of the trainees who were getting kicked out...

286
00:10:21,004 --> 00:10:22,403
were printed out in different colors.

287
00:10:22,404 --> 00:10:23,643
That was the last day of their training.

288
00:10:23,644 --> 00:10:25,473
My agency used to call us separately.

289
00:10:25,474 --> 00:10:26,613
- Separately?
- Yes.

290
00:10:26,614 --> 00:10:29,190
- They called us into their office.
- You got individual consultations.

291
00:10:29,214 --> 00:10:30,783
Listen to these stories. It's so intense.

292
00:10:30,784 --> 00:10:33,153
- They were so young too.
- It wasn't easy. Seriously.

293
00:10:33,154 --> 00:10:35,283
Nowadays, kids train to become idol stars in elementary school.

294
00:10:35,284 --> 00:10:38,164
- Right. There were so many of them.
- Right. I don't think I can do it.

295
00:10:38,324 --> 00:10:42,223
But I'm glad I became a trainee rather late...

296
00:10:42,224 --> 00:10:43,233
now that I think about it.

297
00:10:43,234 --> 00:10:45,833
I went to school up until 11th grade.

298
00:10:45,834 --> 00:10:46,863
She got to experience...

299
00:10:46,864 --> 00:10:48,880
- a normal life with her friends.
- I even went on a school retreat.

300
00:10:48,904 --> 00:10:49,974
That's amazing.

301
00:10:50,204 --> 00:10:52,803
- The school retreat in 11th grade?
- I got to enjoy everything.

302
00:10:52,804 --> 00:10:55,503
When my friends were deciding their majors,

303
00:10:55,504 --> 00:10:57,773
I stopped studying.

304
00:10:57,774 --> 00:11:01,244
They told me that I stopped studying right when it started to get tough.

305
00:11:02,614 --> 00:11:06,083
But you didn't get to experience any college campus life.

306
00:11:06,084 --> 00:11:07,584
- No.
- Right.

307
00:11:07,924 --> 00:11:10,624
College... It's an unknown world for me.

308
00:11:10,754 --> 00:11:12,154
An unknown world.

309
00:11:12,624 --> 00:11:15,093
- Like the orientation trip.
- Right.

310
00:11:15,094 --> 00:11:16,933
- Right.
- Group blind dates.

311
00:11:16,934 --> 00:11:19,254
- The trip and the blind dates...
- It's an unknown world.

312
00:11:19,434 --> 00:11:22,503
We've never heard about or experienced those two activities.

313
00:11:22,504 --> 00:11:23,633
(A world never seen or heard before)

314
00:11:23,634 --> 00:11:25,433
I learned about the group dates and department mixers...

315
00:11:25,434 --> 00:11:27,204
through movies and dramas.

316
00:11:28,004 --> 00:11:29,413
Have you guys done that before?

317
00:11:29,414 --> 00:11:31,744
- Group dates...
- We have some experience.

318
00:11:32,544 --> 00:11:35,383
We've tried that. We handed over our belongings to pick partners.

319
00:11:35,384 --> 00:11:37,753
- I tried that in a drama!
- No way.

320
00:11:37,754 --> 00:11:39,923
- I tried that.
- I missed a few classes,

321
00:11:39,924 --> 00:11:41,284
but I always attended those dates.

322
00:11:43,194 --> 00:11:45,653
I always attended those group dates.

323
00:11:45,654 --> 00:11:46,663
(Observing)

324
00:11:46,664 --> 00:11:49,293
No way. I used to go to that taekwondo studio.

325
00:11:49,294 --> 00:11:50,993
- Where?
- That one over there?

326
00:11:50,994 --> 00:11:53,063
- For a month, though.
- The one over there? Really?

327
00:11:53,064 --> 00:11:54,133
The taekwondo studio.

328
00:11:54,134 --> 00:11:55,203
(Taekwondo Studio)

329
00:11:55,204 --> 00:11:56,603
- That's the studio.
- No way.

330
00:11:56,604 --> 00:11:59,133
You know what? The building does look old enough.

331
00:11:59,134 --> 00:12:01,073
- Right.
- There's a gimbap place I love...

332
00:12:01,074 --> 00:12:02,973
on the first floor.

333
00:12:02,974 --> 00:12:03,974
(Her regular gimbap place is on the 1st floor.)

334
00:12:03,975 --> 00:12:06,013
(Getting more excited as she walks around her town)

335
00:12:06,014 --> 00:12:07,043
That's iffy too.

336
00:12:07,044 --> 00:12:09,753
- Gosh, it's so beautiful.
- Oh, my. So beautiful.

337
00:12:09,754 --> 00:12:10,883
It's a great place to live.

338
00:12:10,884 --> 00:12:13,083
- It's autumn now.
- I keep promoting the town.

339
00:12:13,084 --> 00:12:14,123
(The street filled with autumn vibes)

340
00:12:14,124 --> 00:12:16,193
- Look at the leaves falling.
- It's beautiful.

341
00:12:16,194 --> 00:12:17,224
Already...

342
00:12:17,254 --> 00:12:18,454
I know, right?

343
00:12:18,554 --> 00:12:19,823
It's so beautiful.

344
00:12:19,824 --> 00:12:22,423
- There are a lot of trees here.
- I see.

345
00:12:22,424 --> 00:12:23,664
Oh, how beautiful.

346
00:12:24,434 --> 00:12:26,234
This is great. I want to live here again.

347
00:12:27,564 --> 00:12:32,373
Because Jisoo spent her childhood here,

348
00:12:32,374 --> 00:12:33,773
she's more attached to this place.

349
00:12:33,774 --> 00:12:35,404
- Right. It must be nostalgic.
- Yes.

350
00:12:36,674 --> 00:12:39,913
(Her childhood memories are still preserved in Sanbon.)

351
00:12:39,914 --> 00:12:41,143
It feels great...

352
00:12:41,144 --> 00:12:42,504
- to recognize the streets.
- Yes.

353
00:12:43,184 --> 00:12:46,484
Right. You must be so happy to see your old taekwondo studio.

354
00:12:47,254 --> 00:12:49,353
- Right.
- As she said earlier,

355
00:12:49,354 --> 00:12:50,634
she went there only for a month.

356
00:12:51,424 --> 00:12:53,100
She didn't learn taekwondo there for a long time.

357
00:12:53,124 --> 00:12:54,463
- But taekwondo suits you.
- You're happy to see it, right?

358
00:12:54,464 --> 00:12:57,793
I had a white belt. And I was so happy with it.

359
00:12:57,794 --> 00:12:59,463
- With the white belt?
- After a month,

360
00:12:59,464 --> 00:13:01,163
they said I had to wear a yellow belt.

361
00:13:01,164 --> 00:13:02,303
- Yes.
- So I quit.

362
00:13:02,304 --> 00:13:04,073
- Why?
- She just liked the white belt.

363
00:13:04,074 --> 00:13:06,873
- Oh, you just liked the white belt?
- So when I got the yellow belt...

364
00:13:06,874 --> 00:13:08,974
(The story of why she quit taekwondo after a month)

365
00:13:09,004 --> 00:13:10,413
It looks so beautiful...

366
00:13:10,414 --> 00:13:11,813
- with the sunlight here.
- It's autumn now.

367
00:13:11,814 --> 00:13:13,883
- It's so beautiful.
- It's autumn now.

368
00:13:13,884 --> 00:13:15,014
Do you like winter?

369
00:13:15,214 --> 00:13:17,183
- I prefer winter to summer.
- Me too.

370
00:13:17,184 --> 00:13:20,123
- Really?
- I don't like winter.

371
00:13:20,124 --> 00:13:21,183
When I shoot dramas...

372
00:13:21,184 --> 00:13:22,423
- Isn't it so cold?
- When I shoot dramas...

373
00:13:22,424 --> 00:13:23,853
I'm sure you know since you filmed dramas too.

374
00:13:23,854 --> 00:13:26,093
But I hated filming dramas...

375
00:13:26,094 --> 00:13:27,593
in summer.

376
00:13:27,594 --> 00:13:29,834
- Really?
- The heat in summer...

377
00:13:30,134 --> 00:13:31,994
kind of makes me look ugly.

378
00:13:32,934 --> 00:13:34,833
The thing is, you look prettier in cold weather.

379
00:13:34,834 --> 00:13:36,403
- Oh, yes. That's true.
- When you're cold,

380
00:13:36,404 --> 00:13:39,334
- your face brightens up.
- That's what I heard.

381
00:13:39,844 --> 00:13:41,043
But your lips would get numb.

382
00:13:41,044 --> 00:13:42,603
But the difficult part is that...

383
00:13:42,604 --> 00:13:44,643
we have to move our lips and sing.

384
00:13:44,644 --> 00:13:46,143
On top of that, our breath can't show.

385
00:13:46,144 --> 00:13:47,213
- Really?
- I see.

386
00:13:47,214 --> 00:13:49,574
- We'd have ice cubes in our mouths.
- You'd eat ice cubes.

387
00:13:50,184 --> 00:13:51,904
But can't they use CGI and remove that now?

388
00:13:52,114 --> 00:13:53,723
- Right.
- That's possible now. Right?

389
00:13:53,724 --> 00:13:55,783
(Of course. We can even add it.)

390
00:13:55,784 --> 00:13:56,893
On the right.

391
00:13:56,894 --> 00:13:58,453
Hello.

392
00:13:58,454 --> 00:14:00,494
When I want to go on a trip...

393
00:14:00,864 --> 00:14:02,094
What number is our bus?

394
00:14:02,464 --> 00:14:04,333
- It's Bus 541.
- Bus 541.

395
00:14:04,334 --> 00:14:05,933
- Bus 541 will be here in 3 minutes.
- Which...

396
00:14:05,934 --> 00:14:07,833
- What?
- It will be here in three minutes.

397
00:14:07,834 --> 00:14:09,433
- We can get on Bus 541.
- Yes.

398
00:14:09,434 --> 00:14:11,154
- It will be here in three minutes.
- Okay.

399
00:14:11,234 --> 00:14:13,273
(Chuckling)

400
00:14:13,274 --> 00:14:14,373
Bus 541 will be here in 3 minutes

401
00:14:14,374 --> 00:14:15,543
Three minutes.

402
00:14:15,544 --> 00:14:16,544
(Turning around)

403
00:14:16,545 --> 00:14:18,074
You look a little hyper now.

404
00:14:18,174 --> 00:14:19,244
Yes, I'm excited.

405
00:14:20,314 --> 00:14:21,983
I have to step on a rock in Sanbon.

406
00:14:21,984 --> 00:14:24,153
I think she got hyper when we talked about taekwondo.

407
00:14:24,154 --> 00:14:25,414
She's suddenly excited.

408
00:14:25,554 --> 00:14:27,023
- Now that Jisoo...
- You should step on it.

409
00:14:27,024 --> 00:14:28,583
- is in her hometown...
- Really?

410
00:14:28,584 --> 00:14:29,593
Of course.

411
00:14:29,594 --> 00:14:32,254
The natural landscape in Sanbon is amazing.

412
00:14:32,354 --> 00:14:34,363
We should have fun in a nature-friendly manner.

413
00:14:34,364 --> 00:14:36,364
Nayeon isn't from here. What's she doing up there?

414
00:14:36,594 --> 00:14:38,334
(Giggling)

415
00:14:38,564 --> 00:14:40,934
- Bus 541 is here.
- Bus 541.

416
00:14:41,204 --> 00:14:43,104
- Bus 541.
- It's here.

417
00:14:43,934 --> 00:14:45,773
- Take this.
- Hello.

418
00:14:45,774 --> 00:14:47,003
- At the end.
- At the end.

419
00:14:47,004 --> 00:14:48,074
Hello.

420
00:14:48,174 --> 00:14:49,174
(No passengers on the bus)

421
00:14:49,175 --> 00:14:51,044
- How many stops?
- Yes.

422
00:14:51,474 --> 00:14:53,343
- No one's here like we rented it.
- Exactly.

423
00:14:53,344 --> 00:14:54,543
- But we didn't rent it.
- Why...

424
00:14:54,544 --> 00:14:56,113
- It's like we rented this bus.
- Right.

425
00:14:56,114 --> 00:14:58,454
(Somehow, they ended up having the bus to themselves.)

426
00:14:58,784 --> 00:15:01,104
- Which stop are we getting off at?
- We're getting off...

427
00:15:02,224 --> 00:15:03,754
at the Royal Azalea Hill.

428
00:15:03,994 --> 00:15:05,454
- I see.
- The Royal Azalea Hill.

429
00:15:05,554 --> 00:15:07,663
- Royal azaleas are famous here.
- Really?

430
00:15:07,664 --> 00:15:09,933
- There's an azalea festival too.
- Really?

431
00:15:09,934 --> 00:15:11,363
It's a famous festival.

432
00:15:11,364 --> 00:15:13,003
- They're not in season now.
- Really?

433
00:15:13,004 --> 00:15:14,180
(Showing Sanbon off whenever she gets a chance)

434
00:15:14,204 --> 00:15:16,534
Are you guys good at games?

435
00:15:16,774 --> 00:15:17,804
I like games.

436
00:15:17,904 --> 00:15:19,104
- Really? You do?
- I knew it.

437
00:15:19,374 --> 00:15:21,144
And I'm very competitive.

438
00:15:21,544 --> 00:15:22,703
- Really?
- Yes.

439
00:15:22,704 --> 00:15:24,913
Do you guys play games to pick who buys coffee for the staff?

440
00:15:24,914 --> 00:15:27,144
Yes. I love playing games.

441
00:15:27,684 --> 00:15:29,953
We recently celebrated our 11th anniversary.

442
00:15:29,954 --> 00:15:31,954
So I had a meal with my members.

443
00:15:32,014 --> 00:15:33,924
We kept playing games.

444
00:15:34,384 --> 00:15:36,123
- So you practiced for today.
- We kept playing games.

445
00:15:36,124 --> 00:15:37,253
- We played games nonstop.
- You're like Yeon Shik.

446
00:15:37,254 --> 00:15:40,164
- He plays games all the time.
- For... Yes.

447
00:15:40,564 --> 00:15:42,824
So do you usually win?

448
00:15:43,194 --> 00:15:46,163
I rarely lose at these games.

449
00:15:46,164 --> 00:15:47,234
Really?

450
00:15:48,704 --> 00:15:49,973
Gosh, that's amazing.

451
00:15:49,974 --> 00:15:53,074
I wonder what kind of clip will follow after this.

452
00:15:53,304 --> 00:15:54,680
What if this clip keeps showing up?

453
00:15:54,704 --> 00:15:56,374
"I rarely lose at these games."

454
00:15:56,874 --> 00:15:58,074
What about you, Jisoo?

455
00:15:58,214 --> 00:15:59,313
- Me?
- Yes.

456
00:15:59,314 --> 00:16:01,144
I'm not competitive at all.

457
00:16:02,214 --> 00:16:05,153
But I have a big sense of obligation.

458
00:16:05,154 --> 00:16:06,823
- So...
- I do well when it's for others.

459
00:16:06,824 --> 00:16:08,083
- I work hard then.
- We're similar.

460
00:16:08,084 --> 00:16:10,894
Jisoo and I are similar.

461
00:16:11,024 --> 00:16:12,724
- Nayeon and Yeon Shik are similar.
- Yes.

462
00:16:13,664 --> 00:16:14,964
(Coming up soon)

463
00:16:16,294 --> 00:16:20,734
(The sense of obligation has made Jisoo go wild.)

464
00:16:21,104 --> 00:16:24,074
(Nayeon goes full beast mode on the games.)

465
00:16:24,834 --> 00:16:27,474
(A dopamine rush is coming soon.)

466
00:16:28,344 --> 00:16:30,444
- Wait. Where's Royal Azalea Hill?
- I screamed.

467
00:16:30,714 --> 00:16:32,544
- Is this it? We have to get off.
- Wait.

468
00:16:32,844 --> 00:16:34,183
We almost missed our stop.

469
00:16:34,184 --> 00:16:35,243
Thank you, sir.

470
00:16:35,244 --> 00:16:36,753
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

471
00:16:36,754 --> 00:16:38,113
I can't believe...

472
00:16:38,114 --> 00:16:40,053
- no one was on the bus.
- I know, right?

473
00:16:40,054 --> 00:16:42,283
- It's a city bus too.
- I thought they rented it for us.

474
00:16:42,284 --> 00:16:43,694
No one was on the bus.

475
00:16:43,824 --> 00:16:46,093
- They'll wait for us on a bench.
- What?

476
00:16:46,094 --> 00:16:47,224
On a bench.

477
00:16:47,494 --> 00:16:50,163
- A bench at the Royal Azalea Hill.
- A bench?

478
00:16:50,164 --> 00:16:51,764
There's a map of the park.

479
00:16:52,394 --> 00:16:54,164
They'll wait for us on a bench?

480
00:16:55,034 --> 00:16:56,134
Well...

481
00:16:56,404 --> 00:16:58,403
- I see 2 people and 3 people.
- Where are they? I see 3 people.

482
00:16:58,404 --> 00:16:59,673
- I see three people there too.
- It's over there.

483
00:16:59,674 --> 00:17:01,674
- I think it's over there.
- It's over there.

484
00:17:02,044 --> 00:17:04,073
- They're standing up so straight.
- They're already looking at us.

485
00:17:04,074 --> 00:17:05,274
They're already smiling.

486
00:17:05,614 --> 00:17:07,694
- They're already...
- I can already feel the vibes.

487
00:17:07,784 --> 00:17:09,143
- sneaking peeks at us.
- Yes.

488
00:17:09,144 --> 00:17:11,314
They're getting ready. They look nervous.

489
00:17:11,484 --> 00:17:12,784
Hello.

490
00:17:12,914 --> 00:17:14,354
Hello.

491
00:17:14,484 --> 00:17:15,683
(Surprised)

492
00:17:15,684 --> 00:17:17,394
- Hello.
- Hello.

493
00:17:17,724 --> 00:17:18,893
- Hello.
- No way.

494
00:17:18,894 --> 00:17:21,594
- Hello.
- We usually meet up in offices.

